Directed joins of ideal elements presented by an index type, and preservation of those joins by approximable maps.

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`iSupDirected`).** The directed supremum of a nonempty directed family of ideal elements, presented as a function on an index type, is the directed join of the range of that function.

**Theorem (`mem_iSupDirected`).** A neighbourhood belongs to the indexed directed supremum if and only if it belongs to some term of the family.

**Theorem (`iSupDirected_le`).** The indexed directed supremum is below any common upper bound of the family.

**Theorem (`le_iSupDirected`).** Each term of the family is below the indexed directed supremum.

**Theorem (`toElementMap_iSupDirected`).** The elementwise action of an approximable map preserves indexed directed suprema.

*Proof.* Membership in the image of the join is membership for some term, transported by the defining formula for the elementwise action. ∎
